# Panoptes-macOS — netcheck: read installed configuration profiles.
# arp-scan is NOT here by default: with free arguments it can write files as root
# (-W), and in a Homebrew prefix the binary itself is user-replaceable — either is a
# root escalation, so netcheck/nettop simply prompt for it. install.sh appends a rule
# only when arp-scan and every directory above it are root-owned (MacPorts), and only
# for the exact argument lists netcheck and nettop use (interface pinned to en<N>).
@USER@ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/profiles show -type configuration
